=== 3. the 3x+1 kernel: moduli N prime to 6 with an involutive branch ===
   N < 2000: [(5, 'o')]    (o^2 = id  <=>  (3/2)^2 = 1  <=>  N | 3^2 - 2^2 = 5;  e^2 = id  <=>  N | 3)
   so 5 = 3^2 - 2^2 = 3 + 2 is the only modulus at which a branch of the 3x+1 map is an involution: there 3/2 = -1, the odd branch is a reflection,
   and the word 'oo' (the cell (k, s) = (2, 2) of the exponent lattice, 2^2 - 3^2 = -5) is the identity.

